          "title": "wp-content/plugins/plugin-a/plugin-a.php:8",
          "detail": "no automatic patch: not custom code (unknown: not inside any customPaths entry: ownership is not assumed (a plugin name or location does not prove it is custom). Add it to customPaths to allow fix tasks.)",
          "verification": []
        },
        {
          "type": "patch",
          "who": "send-to-claude-code",
          "title": "Wrap function my_helper() in a function_exists() guard",
          "detail": "my_helper is declared here and also elsewhere; if both files load, PHP stops with \"Cannot redeclare\". The guard makes the first one that loads win. It does NOT decide which copy should win: that is a decision for the owner (see the other resolution options). Note that a guarded function is defined when the line runs, not at compile time.",
          "file": "wp-content/plugins/plugin-b/plugin-b.php",
          "line": 8,
          "generator": "function-guard",
          "diff": "--- a/wp-content/plugins/plugin-b/plugin-b.php\n+++ b/wp-content/plugins/plugin-b/plugin-b.php\n@@ -5,8 +5,10 @@\n  */\n defined( 'ABSPATH' ) || exit;\n \n-function my_helper( $x ) {\n-\treturn $x . 'b';\n+if ( ! function_exists( 'my_helper' ) ) {\n+\tfunction my_helper( $x ) {\n+\t\treturn $x . 'b';\n+\t}\n }\n add_filter( 'the_title', 'my_helper' );\n \n",
          "verification": [
